title: Tram — a controlled line out and back (ADR-366 D5a, D5e)
story: vehicles
description: The tram car runs its three stops under a brake at a pace of
  two turns, halting at each end; a second push at the Terminus runs it
  back. The funicular is the same line one way: at its end a further start
  does nothing.

---

> north
[OK: contains "Depot"]

> enter tram car
[OK: contains "get into the tram car"]

# start puts it under way; the sequence anchored on `becomes under way` fires
> push brake
[OK: contains "The brake comes off."]
[OK: contains "The tram car lurches into motion."]

# pace: 2 turns — the start turn's tick counts, the step lands next turn
> wait
[OK: contains "The tram car arrives at the Midway Halt."]

# Every turn ticks the pace: this look is one of the two
> look
[OK: contains "Midway Halt"]

> wait
[OK: contains "The tram car arrives at the Terminus."]

# Halted at the end: nothing moves
> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

# The run back (a sequence is a progression: its anchor step fired once and does not re-arm)
> push brake
[OK: contains "The brake comes off."]
[OK: not contains "lurches"]

> wait
[OK: contains "The tram car arrives at the Midway Halt."]

> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

> wait
[OK: contains "The tram car arrives at the Depot."]

> exit
[OK: contains "You get out of the tram car."]

# The one-way funicular
